🎭 Actors
Job Seeker: Registers, searches jobs, applies, uploads resume.

Recruiter/Employer: Posts jobs, reviews applications, schedules interviews.

System Administrator: Manages users, maintains system integrity.

Payment Gateway (optional): Handles premium job postings or paid services.

📌 Use Cases (Messages/Interactions)
Register Account: Actor creates profile.

Login: Access system with credentials.

Search Jobs: Job seeker browses available postings.

Apply for Job: Submit application with resume.

Upload Resume: Attach CV to profile.

Post Job: Recruiter creates new job listing.

Review Applications: Recruiter checks candidate submissions.

Schedule Interview: Recruiter arranges interview with candidate.

Manage Users: Admin oversees accounts.

Payment Processing: Employer pays for premium services.

🔗 Relationships (Include / Extend)
Login → include → Register Account (if new user).

Apply for Job → include → Upload Resume (resume required).

Post Job → include → Payment Processing (if premium posting).

Schedule Interview → extend → Review Applications (only if candidate is shortlisted).

Search Jobs → extend → Filter Jobs (optional refinement).

